WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:00.767
OUTFRONT now.

00:00:00.767 --> 00:00:01.668
Konstantin Yefremov,

00:00:01.668 --> 00:00:02.802
the former Russian

00:00:02.802 --> 00:00:03.670
senior lieutenant

00:00:03.670 --> 00:00:04.270
who is seeking

00:00:04.270 --> 00:00:05.238
asylum in the US

00:00:05.238 --> 00:00:06.840
after serving in Ukraine.

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:08.174
He is the most senior officer

00:00:08.174 --> 00:00:10.510
to speak openly about what he saw there.

00:00:11.011 --> 00:00:12.779
And Konstantin, I appreciate your time.

00:00:12.779 --> 00:00:13.980
You shared with us

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:15.749
your military ID card,

00:00:15.749 --> 00:00:16.483
which I'm

00:00:16.483 --> 00:00:17.817
going to show viewers on the screen

00:00:17.817 --> 00:00:18.685
now that shows

00:00:18.685 --> 00:00:22.222
you were made a lieutenant in 2017

00:00:22.655 --> 00:00:24.991
and obviously you served in Ukraine.

00:00:25.425 --> 00:00:26.459
I know you still speak

00:00:26.459 --> 00:00:27.360
with Russian soldiers

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:29.229
who are there fighting now.

00:00:29.229 --> 00:00:30.897
What are they telling you about

00:00:30.897 --> 00:00:33.233
what's happening on the ground?

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:34.100
Sochi.

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:35.702
Mullen College, Columbia.

00:00:35.702 --> 00:00:36.970
Well, I have to say that

00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:38.705
there are only very few people

00:00:38.705 --> 00:00:40.907
that I have been in contact with

00:00:40.907 --> 00:00:42.208
because you can imagine

00:00:42.208 --> 00:00:44.277
just talking to me is already

00:00:44.711 --> 00:00:45.879
that puts them

00:00:45.879 --> 00:00:47.981
at the risk of high danger.

00:00:47.981 --> 00:00:48.681
In fact,

00:00:48.681 --> 00:00:49.983
after this interview

00:00:49.983 --> 00:00:51.184
and just opening up,

00:00:51.184 --> 00:00:53.053
I can imagine tomorrow

00:00:53.053 --> 00:00:55.021
or may just as well even today,

00:00:55.021 --> 00:00:56.689
they will start talking to me.

00:00:56.689 --> 00:00:59.259
And the last time I talked to them,

00:00:59.626 --> 00:01:00.260
there wasn't much

00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:01.227
they could share with me.

00:01:01.227 --> 00:01:03.296
Just hunger cold.

00:01:03.663 --> 00:01:05.131
They're their circumstances.

00:01:05.131 --> 00:01:06.599
Their conditions are very dire.

00:01:07.901 --> 00:01:09.569
You talk about dire conditions.

00:01:09.569 --> 00:01:10.737
And I know you shared with us

00:01:10.737 --> 00:01:11.571
some photos,

00:01:11.571 --> 00:01:12.672
Konstantin, that you say

00:01:12.672 --> 00:01:15.041
are from your time fighting in Ukraine.

00:01:15.041 --> 00:01:17.010
And we've heard

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:18.144
you talk about them being hungry.

00:01:18.144 --> 00:01:19.446
We hear about Russian soldiers

00:01:19.446 --> 00:01:20.380
not having enough food

00:01:20.380 --> 00:01:21.781
that happened to you.

00:01:21.781 --> 00:01:23.116
You took a picture of this rabbit

00:01:23.116 --> 00:01:24.918
that you had to hunt for food

00:01:24.918 --> 00:01:25.652
while you were there,

00:01:25.652 --> 00:01:26.419
and then you boiled it

00:01:26.419 --> 00:01:27.353
in a bucket to eat.

00:01:27.353 --> 00:01:30.356
And you sent us that photo as well.

00:01:30.356 --> 00:01:31.224
What is morale

00:01:31.224 --> 00:01:32.892
like right now for the troops?

00:01:32.892 --> 00:01:36.062
I know you're describing it as dire

00:01:36.162 --> 00:01:38.298
physical on the hood of

00:01:38.298 --> 00:01:40.633
everyone or nearly everyone

00:01:40.633 --> 00:01:42.268
who is there and a sense

00:01:42.268 --> 00:01:45.338
that what's happening is wrong,

00:01:45.338 --> 00:01:46.773
that it's all very wrong

00:01:46.773 --> 00:01:48.208
and they truly do not believe

00:01:48.208 --> 00:01:50.043
Putin's fables about

00:01:51.344 --> 00:01:53.646
Ukraine's threat of invasion.

00:01:53.646 --> 00:01:55.682
And I'd like to say that

00:01:55.949 --> 00:01:57.617
the very fact that they are in trenches

00:01:57.617 --> 00:01:59.352
and was just caused

00:01:59.352 --> 00:02:01.521
by their living situation,

00:02:01.521 --> 00:02:03.957
for many of them, their military service

00:02:04.157 --> 00:02:07.827
is their means of living and basically

00:02:07.827 --> 00:02:09.262
they only have one choice.

00:02:09.262 --> 00:02:10.430
It's either

00:02:10.497 --> 00:02:11.464
they are family

00:02:11.464 --> 00:02:13.800
and children end up on the streets

00:02:13.967 --> 00:02:16.202
or they have to be in the trenches

00:02:16.803 --> 00:02:19.806
and now after the after the mobilization,

00:02:20.140 --> 00:02:21.407
many of them

00:02:21.407 --> 00:02:22.008
in general

00:02:22.008 --> 00:02:23.042
after the mobilization,

00:02:23.042 --> 00:02:25.111
they cannot even resign.

00:02:25.712 --> 00:02:27.280
And otherwise

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:28.781
they'll be sent to prison

00:02:28.781 --> 00:02:30.450
for seven, ten years.

00:02:30.450 --> 00:02:32.685
So basically, there is no choice.

00:02:32.986 --> 00:02:35.021
They either have to

00:02:35.021 --> 00:02:38.258
remain there or find ways to flee.

00:02:38.658 --> 00:02:40.693
So like I've already said,

00:02:40.693 --> 00:02:42.395
the circumstances are dire

00:02:42.395 --> 00:02:44.631
and it usually or sealed up if

00:02:44.697 --> 00:02:45.732
sort of necessary. Army

00:02:46.866 --> 00:02:47.200
You know,

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:48.835
obviously some of what

00:02:48.835 --> 00:02:49.936
has happened on the ground,

00:02:49.936 --> 00:02:50.103
you know,

00:02:50.103 --> 00:02:51.804
we know about horrific

00:02:51.804 --> 00:02:52.539
war crimes

00:02:52.539 --> 00:02:53.473
committed

00:02:53.473 --> 00:02:54.841
by Russian forces

00:02:54.841 --> 00:02:56.843
across the entire state of this war.

00:02:57.243 --> 00:02:59.045
You shared a video or photo

00:02:59.045 --> 00:03:00.880
with us in front of a building in Ukraine

00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:01.481
where you say that

00:03:01.481 --> 00:03:04.117
Ukrainian prisoners were tortured.

00:03:05.018 --> 00:03:07.287
What did you see happen

00:03:09.222 --> 00:03:10.290
Yeah, we do.

00:03:10.590 --> 00:03:12.058
I personally

00:03:12.058 --> 00:03:14.527
saw how the deputy commander of the unit,

00:03:14.794 --> 00:03:17.430
whose name is Schaitberger, tortured

00:03:17.830 --> 00:03:20.400
and threatened with sexual violence,

00:03:21.301 --> 00:03:24.237
prisoners of war from the 36

00:03:24.437 --> 00:03:25.939
Navy Division.

00:03:25.939 --> 00:03:27.974
Were there others?

00:03:27.974 --> 00:03:31.077
Konstantin who had issues with this?

00:03:32.378 --> 00:03:34.047
Because obviously many soldiers

00:03:34.047 --> 00:03:36.349
were participating in going along

00:03:38.818 --> 00:03:39.085
Yeah.

00:03:39.085 --> 00:03:40.753
And I cannot say that

00:03:40.753 --> 00:03:44.090
anyone would have dared to say anything

00:03:44.490 --> 00:03:45.992
to this Colonel

00:03:45.992 --> 00:03:47.160
in any way

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:48.561
or could have showed

00:03:48.561 --> 00:03:49.796
their disapproval anything.

00:03:49.796 --> 00:03:51.664
Because just like he shot

00:03:51.664 --> 00:03:54.100
that Ukrainian prisoner of war,

00:03:54.100 --> 00:03:56.169
he could have easily shot me

00:03:56.169 --> 00:03:57.403
or anyone else

00:03:57.403 --> 00:03:58.104
who said that

00:03:58.104 --> 00:03:59.305
they didn't agree with this.

00:03:59.305 --> 00:04:02.609
Besides, he was drunk nonstop,

00:04:02.609 --> 00:04:04.711
and he was driving around

00:04:05.612 --> 00:04:06.946
the nearby villages

00:04:06.946 --> 00:04:09.916
where there were other prisoners of war.

00:04:10.350 --> 00:04:12.318
As far as I know, there were about

00:04:12.318 --> 00:04:15.054
20 others, Ukrainian prisoners or boys.

00:04:15.421 --> 00:04:16.589
But I myself

00:04:16.589 --> 00:04:19.626
and was a witness of interrogations

00:04:19.659 --> 00:04:22.428
of three Ukrainian prisoners of war.

00:04:22.962 --> 00:04:24.163
You tried to resign,

00:04:24.163 --> 00:04:25.665
Konstantin, from the army.

00:04:25.665 --> 00:04:26.799
You ended up being dismissed

00:04:26.799 --> 00:04:29.035
because you refused to return to Ukraine.

00:04:29.035 --> 00:04:30.870
And they sent you a document.

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:31.771
You shared it with us.

00:04:31.771 --> 00:04:32.905
And let me just read part of it

00:04:32.905 --> 00:04:34.240
to our viewers.

00:04:34.240 --> 00:04:35.408
This serviceman refused

00:04:35.408 --> 00:04:36.743
to go to the territory of Ukraine

00:04:36.743 --> 00:04:38.911
to perform his service in combat mission.

00:04:38.911 --> 00:04:40.380
Thereby, senior lieutenant

00:04:40.380 --> 00:04:40.713
from up

00:04:40.713 --> 00:04:42.415
Konstantin Vladimirovich,

00:04:42.415 --> 00:04:44.284
committed a gross disciplinary offense

00:04:44.284 --> 00:04:45.652
expressed by his evasion

00:04:45.652 --> 00:04:47.987
from his duties of military service.

00:04:48.554 --> 00:04:49.022
Konstantin,

00:04:49.022 --> 00:04:50.790
you are now hoping to seek asylum

00:04:50.790 --> 00:04:51.724
in the United States.

00:04:51.724 --> 00:04:52.892
You have left Russia.

00:04:53.893 --> 00:04:54.294
Why do you

00:04:54.294 --> 00:04:54.827
think the United

00:04:54.827 --> 00:04:57.397
States should grant you asylum Yes.

00:04:57.397 --> 00:04:58.731
First, Sascha,

00:04:58.731 --> 00:05:01.401
if a strong that is democracy,

00:05:02.502 --> 00:05:03.303
I believe that

00:05:03.303 --> 00:05:06.239
the United States of America

00:05:06.239 --> 00:05:08.308
is the country of democracy

00:05:08.541 --> 00:05:10.443
where human rights are upheld.

00:05:10.443 --> 00:05:12.712
And I've already been in Mexico for

00:05:13.279 --> 00:05:13.880
a month.

00:05:13.880 --> 00:05:15.348
And over this period of time,

00:05:15.348 --> 00:05:18.117
I've been trying to

00:05:18.117 --> 00:05:20.386
seek an appointment

00:05:20.386 --> 00:05:21.721
with the border guards.

00:05:21.721 --> 00:05:23.856
And unfortunately,

00:05:23.856 --> 00:05:25.692
so far, my efforts have been in vain.

00:05:25.692 --> 00:05:27.927
And therefore, I'm

00:05:28.695 --> 00:05:29.228
I addressed

00:05:29.228 --> 00:05:30.763
mass media and human rights

00:05:30.763 --> 00:05:32.332
advocates, advocates

00:05:32.332 --> 00:05:35.001
to support me in seeking political asylum

00:05:35.568 --> 00:05:37.904
items, to pursue political leadership

00:05:38.638 --> 00:05:39.605
Konstantin, thank you

00:05:39.605 --> 00:05:42.408
so very much for your time.

00:05:42.408 --> 00:05:42.842
----

